,"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n Reproducible in: v4.7\n Worked correctly in: 4.6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1062) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700K (24 threads) - 31.77 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\n Selecting a scene tab (single click on the tab for a whole scene) causes the configured external script editor (VS Code) to open and steal focus, when the scene's root node has a C# script attached. This happens on every scene switch, not just when I deliberately open a script.\n\n  This is a regression. The behavior was fixed by PR #40735\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n  1. Use a C# (.NET) project with an external editor configured for C# (VS).\n  2. Have at least two scenes open one of whose root nodes has a C# script attached.\n  3. Double click on the scene with a script once.\n  4. Single-click the scene tab to switch scenes.\n  5. Observe: VS opens/gains focus automatically, without double-clicking any script.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A any new project has this issue","closed_by":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ki